03:53:31.100 --> 03:53:37.100
Not so much to watch out, although some people said, Hey, I got your back.

03:53:37.100 --> 03:53:43.100
If somebody messes with you, I got your back.

03:53:43.100 --> 03:53:53.100
We were warned that maybe we would not have friendly other legislators that would be friendly towards me or towards my colleague.

03:53:53.100 --> 03:53:59.100
And for the most part, I've been welcomed.

03:53:59.100 --> 03:54:07.100
But there was one day when I was walking through the Capitol and there were a group of women legislators.

03:54:07.100 --> 03:54:13.100
And overheard them say, I don't have a problem with the LGBT.

03:54:13.100 --> 03:54:17.100
Oh, excuse me. I don't have a problem with the LGBT.

03:54:17.100 --> 03:54:21.100
But I have a problem with the T.

03:54:21.100 --> 03:54:35.100
And since 2019, these kinds of bills have been coming up against the transgender community.

03:54:35.100 --> 03:54:46.100
It feels to me that this bill is targeted to a specific person, specific legislator in our community.

03:54:46.100 --> 03:54:50.100
And it's wrong.

03:54:50.100 --> 03:54:58.100
I think it's very discriminatory.

03:54:58.100 --> 03:55:06.100
It's very hurtful.

03:55:06.100 --> 03:55:15.100
And it feels like a retaliatory act.

03:55:15.100 --> 03:55:22.100
I urge you to vote no on SB 244. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

03:55:22.100 --> 03:55:31.100
Does any other member wish to speak to the bill? The chair recognizes representative Featherston.

03:55:31.100 --> 03:55:34.100
Sorry, I represent just a moment.

03:55:34.100 --> 03:55:41.100
The chair recognizes represent Adam Smith for an announcement first. I apologize.

03:55:41.100 --> 03:55:49.100
Thank you, Mr. Chair. Just a quick announcement. House taxation has been postponed until next week. So there's no house tax this afternoon.

03:55:49.100 --> 03:55:54.100
Now the chair recognizes represent Featherston. I apologize.

03:55:54.100 --> 03:56:00.100
Thank you, Mr. Chair.

03:56:00.100 --> 03:56:10.100
So in 1961, the people of Kansas had a constitutional amendment in which they voted for local control.

03:56:10.100 --> 03:56:21.100
We make a big deal about that in this chamber and in this building. Local control respect our local entities.

03:56:21.100 --> 03:56:38.100
This bill violates that respect we have for our local entities, just like the entire process of this bill coming to this floor today violated the trust that our constituents have put in us.

03:56:38.100 --> 03:56:48.100
My community, especially the business community, prides itself on being a welcoming community and they hear directly from our business community.

03:56:48.100 --> 03:56:54.100
People want to move to my town because we welcome everybody.

03:56:54.100 --> 03:57:06.100
This bill inhibits my city's ability to grow and for us to live in peace.

03:57:06.100 --> 03:57:19.100
I did have the opportunity to step out during this hearing today to talk to my city to see what they did feel concerned about.

03:57:19.100 --> 03:57:25.100
These are the things that my city is concerned about and I think probably also yours.

03:57:25.100 --> 03:57:29.100
I don't find any of them addressed in this bill.

03:57:29.100 --> 03:57:39.100
It's causing affordable health care, affordable child care, property tax reduction, especially for our seniors.

03:57:39.100 --> 03:57:48.100
Fully funding special education, fully funding our schools, having a livable minimum wage.

03:57:48.100 --> 03:57:51.100
Most of all, my city is concerned.

03:57:51.100 --> 03:57:57.100
Are we doing anything up here to make life better for any Kansas at all?

03:57:57.100 --> 03:58:00.100
As I think so far, I write a newsletter every week.

03:58:00.100 --> 03:58:03.100
And every week, I'm like, I got nothing good to tell you.

03:58:03.100 --> 03:58:13.100
Nothing has come across this floor that helped anybody, although I will say the AG bills that crossed the floor today that went through another committee.

03:58:13.100 --> 03:58:16.100
I do think those helped somebody. So thanks for that.

03:58:16.100 --> 03:58:27.100
But I'm tired of writing to my constituents and say, I'm wasting your tax dollars being up here, except I'm not because I'm standing on the right side of history.

03:58:27.100 --> 03:58:31.100
So this bill is supposed to be about privacy.

03:58:31.100 --> 03:58:40.100
Well, in my town, and I would suspect many of yours, we actually call non gendered bathrooms privacy bathrooms.

03:58:40.100 --> 03:58:48.100
So we got it covered. If you can't cover that in your city, okay, you do you, but we got it covered.

03:58:48.100 --> 03:58:52.100
We know their privacy bathrooms. We like that door all the way to the floor.

03:58:52.100 --> 03:59:02.100
We like to be efficient. We like to bring our kids in, grandkids, you know, we don't want to be kidnapped or human trafficked because we couldn't bring them into the bathroom with us.

03:59:02.100 --> 03:59:05.100
But I guess that's another point.

03:59:05.100 --> 03:59:09.100
This bill is also supposed to be about protecting women.

03:59:09.100 --> 03:59:20.100
Something that really would protect women that this body did pass is expansion of mammogram coverage.

03:59:20.100 --> 03:59:23.100
Remember, we had a long discussion about it. We passed it.

03:59:23.100 --> 03:59:29.100
And leadership on one end just had to kill that over and over and over.

03:59:29.100 --> 03:59:34.100
We'll get to talk about it again, though, this year, don't you worry.

03:59:34.100 --> 03:59:42.100
Finally, I think there are a lot of days we pass things like don't make a big deal in people's lives.

03:59:42.100 --> 03:59:51.100
They make a big deal in somebody's lives, but they're, you know, it's kind of down the middle. That's great. No big deal.

03:59:51.100 --> 04:00:02.100
But there are days like today where I have to really question the state of my soul for being around this kind of ugly talk and hatefulness.

04:00:02.100 --> 04:00:09.100
This bill does real harm to Kansas families.

04:00:09.100 --> 04:00:26.100
I have never had to text a constituent over a bill to say, please prepare yourself for the worst, except for earlier unconstitutional, by the way, versions of this bill.

04:00:26.100 --> 04:00:36.100
And it does not make me proud to have to text my constituents and tell them I have nothing to say.

04:00:36.100 --> 04:00:40.100
I don't know how to tell you to protect your child.

04:00:40.100 --> 04:00:52.100
And I didn't come up here to hurt families. I sure as heck didn't come up here to hurt kids who have no voice.

04:00:52.100 --> 04:01:07.100
I'm not here to harass people who make up such a small percentage of our population that you could barely pick a handful out of a crowd.

04:01:07.100 --> 04:01:24.100
So I would urge you to vote no on this and to stop harming Kansas families, stop wasting taxpayer dollars, and let's do something that actually helps our people.

04:01:24.100 --> 04:01:26.100
Thank you, Mr. Chair.

04:01:26.100 --> 04:01:40.100
Does any other member wish to speak to the bill? The Chair recognizes Representative Meyer.

04:01:40.100 --> 04:01:41.100
Thank you, Mr. Chair.

04:01:41.100 --> 04:01:43.100
Hi, everyone.

04:01:43.100 --> 04:01:47.100
That you were waiting on me to come up here, huh? It's been a minute.

04:01:47.100 --> 04:01:54.100
So to start, I would like to clarify some language that some of the members of the body have been using.

04:01:54.100 --> 04:02:01.100
I want to remind you that transgender men are men. Transgender women are women.

04:02:01.100 --> 04:02:09.100
So when they're walking into that restroom, oh, I love how you're smiling. Great. Wonderful.

04:02:09.100 --> 04:02:18.100
When they're walking into that restroom, as one of my colleagues stated, with a full beard, fully looking like a dude,

04:02:18.100 --> 04:02:25.100
or when they're in there with their big breasts and cleavage everywhere in the women's restroom,

04:02:25.100 --> 04:02:30.100
you're going to say, hey, pull down your pants. Let me see what you got in there. Is that what we're going to do?

04:02:30.100 --> 04:02:36.100
I don't believe that you are a man or a woman. I mean, who's going to do that?

04:02:36.100 --> 04:02:39.100
Just wanted to remind you.

04:02:39.100 --> 04:02:42.100
And I mean, I'll come back to that point.

04:02:42.100 --> 04:02:55.100
But to get serious again, I want to remind you also that people of the transgender community are four times more likely to be a victim of a violent assault.

04:02:55.100 --> 04:02:59.100
That's fat. Oh, are we laughing at that too? That's cool.

04:02:59.100 --> 04:03:15.100
To a previous representatives point about her sexual assault, and you are so brave for sharing that with us. Thank you.

04:03:15.100 --> 04:03:22.100
Many of us have experienced that. Many of us have experienced sexual assault or sexual harassment.

04:03:22.100 --> 04:03:28.100
We don't talk about it. We don't report it because we know who's really going to hurt.

04:03:28.100 --> 04:03:33.100
And it's going to be the survivor, right? The survivor loses everything.

04:03:33.100 --> 04:03:40.100
Did you know that over 99% of the perpetrators of sexual assault are cisgender men?

04:03:40.100 --> 04:03:42.100
Google it.

04:03:42.100 --> 04:03:48.100
I think I said this a couple years ago when we were having a conversation about another one of these asinine bills.

04:03:49.100 --> 04:03:57.100
That you need to be calling out the men around you for their behavior.

04:03:57.100 --> 04:04:00.100
For the fact that they raped women.

04:04:00.100 --> 04:04:03.100
For the fact that they sexually assault children.

04:04:03.100 --> 04:04:11.100
For the fact that they do any of these number of things that you all are inventing happen on a regular basis with transgender individuals.

04:04:11.100 --> 04:04:14.100
Because the facts don't support that either.

04:04:14.100 --> 04:04:18.100
And I think you've heard all of this thing that today. I know we're tired of the debate.

04:04:18.100 --> 04:04:23.100
But you guys are bringing the bills. We're just trying to protect people.

04:04:23.100 --> 04:04:26.100
And back to that.

04:04:26.100 --> 04:04:34.100
The issue you are trying to solve is with rape culture with toxic masculinity.

04:04:34.100 --> 04:04:38.100
With red-pilled young men and older men.

04:04:38.100 --> 04:04:46.100
With the patriarchal power structure that enables men to continue to get away with sexual assault.

04:04:46.100 --> 04:04:52.100
That's what we should be addressing. Not making up an issue because somebody is uncomfortable.

04:04:52.100 --> 04:04:56.100
Because somebody is triggered.

04:04:56.100 --> 04:05:00.100
I've been here. What is this? Five years now? Every single year.

04:05:00.100 --> 04:05:03.100
We've had something like this come up.

04:05:03.100 --> 04:05:05.100
For what?

04:05:05.100 --> 04:05:11.100
Because people have a personal vendetta against a group. Because you're discriminating.

04:05:11.100 --> 04:05:18.100
This whole hearing process was ridiculous. What hearing? Right?

04:05:18.100 --> 04:05:25.100
We don't allow people to come in and share their thoughts and speak their mind. We don't take this seriously.

04:05:25.100 --> 04:05:33.100
And then I'd like to address some other things that a member said earlier about transgender children.

04:05:33.100 --> 04:05:39.100
And cisgender children in the school setting. And how uncomfortable they are.

04:05:39.100 --> 04:05:43.100
So as you all know from my years of talking about this.

04:05:43.100 --> 04:05:48.100
I have a child who's gendered on conforming. Right?

04:05:48.100 --> 04:05:54.100
They are more uncomfortable than the cisgender children that she was talking about.

04:05:55.100 --> 04:06:04.100
I don't even believe that that's something that they feel. I mean, I understand that community doesn't really have a lot of out transgendered children, but mine does.

04:06:06.100 --> 04:06:13.100
And in my community, those trans kids are worried and they're scared for their safety. I get calls from these kids.

04:06:13.100 --> 04:06:21.100
I get letters. I get emails constantly from these kids and their family members saying we are afraid for our future.

04:06:21.100 --> 04:06:29.100
We don't feel comfortable in settings that discriminated against us, that force us to use bathrooms that don't align with our gender identity.

04:06:29.100 --> 04:06:36.100
They know. And then why are we doing this to adults? I mean, this is ridiculous.

04:06:36.100 --> 04:06:41.100
I really truly debate. I'm sorry.

04:06:41.100 --> 04:06:49.100
I just don't think that the claims that the previous representative made about cisgender children feeling uncomfortable are truly that valid.

04:06:49.100 --> 04:06:58.100
And I'd like to see some more information on that, frankly.

04:06:58.100 --> 04:07:03.100
This is a hard day, everyone. I know we're tired.

04:07:03.100 --> 04:07:06.100
But I want you to think about something else, too.

04:07:06.100 --> 04:07:15.100
When we're talking about survivors of sexual assault, what would happen if an individual,

04:07:15.100 --> 04:07:21.100
you know, we don't know if they really need to find out if they're using the right bathroom for their gender identity or not.

04:07:21.100 --> 04:07:34.100
But it seems to me that folks might take this opportunity to further traumatize someone who had been a victim of sexual abuse or sexual assault or sexual harassment through saying,

04:07:34.100 --> 04:07:42.100
you're saying, hey, I don't believe you're really a woman or a man, pull down your pants and let me see what you got.

04:07:42.100 --> 04:07:46.100
No, but that's what's going to happen.

04:07:46.100 --> 04:08:03.100
You can't tell me that you're going to look again, a man with a full beard, walking into a women's restroom and say, yeah, okay, I mean, I think we're trying to do the opposite, right?

04:08:03.100 --> 04:08:07.100
You don't want men with beards in women's spaces, right? But now you're doing it.

04:08:07.100 --> 04:08:11.100
They could have a penis, too. They may have had surgery.

04:08:11.100 --> 04:08:17.100
But according to this bill, it doesn't matter. So you still got penises in there.

04:08:17.100 --> 04:08:23.100
Still got vaginas in the men's room. I mean, hey, think about it.

04:08:23.100 --> 04:08:30.100
Just doesn't make sense.

04:08:30.100 --> 04:08:35.100
I just, and that's the part I can't get over. How is this going to be enforced? Who's going to check?

04:08:35.100 --> 04:08:41.100
Who's going to stand out that bathroom door and tell me, pull down your pants? Let me see.

04:08:41.100 --> 04:08:46.100
You know? Literally.

04:08:46.100 --> 04:08:51.100
I don't know. I'm tired of this conversation.

04:08:51.100 --> 04:08:58.100
But if we want to talk about women's rights, why don't we talk about that, too, since that was a big point someone brought up.

04:08:58.100 --> 04:09:12.100
It doesn't protect women and girls. It weaponizes women's rights and uses this to invalidate people at the core of their humanity.

04:09:12.100 --> 04:09:17.100
And it creates so many legal problems in the long term.

04:09:17.100 --> 04:09:23.100
You can't even run away from that. So, you know, we're talking about we don't have a fiscal note on this.

04:09:23.100 --> 04:09:31.100
Well, we should probably include how much this is going to cost some legal fees, too, because this is, it's a lawsuit waiting to happen.

04:09:31.100 --> 04:09:34.100
I mean, we're waiting on it. Bring it.

04:09:34.100 --> 04:09:41.100
This bill is based on lies and misinformation, and it feeds into stereotypes, and you all know how I feel about it.

04:09:41.100 --> 04:09:49.100
I've made my point, but I want you to continue to consider the impact that this has on the people that you were saying that you were trying to protect.

04:09:49.100 --> 04:10:00.100
This will impact sexual assault survivors. This will impact children. This will impact women. This will impact men at a level that I don't think anyone is really considering.

04:10:00.100 --> 04:10:10.100
And as I said, who's going to ask us to take down our pants? How is this going to be enforced? How is this not sexual assault and battery to ask to do so anyway?

04:10:10.100 --> 04:10:15.100
I mean, we're talking about survivors. We're back to that.

04:10:15.100 --> 04:10:17.100
I'll just end it with this.

04:10:17.100 --> 04:10:29.100
I am really, really exhausted by this conversation, and I know that our community members, especially those who are the most marginalized and disenfranchised, are even more exhausted.

04:10:29.100 --> 04:10:35.100
I came out here to fight for our communities, and that's what I'm doing, and that's why I'm up here every single time.

04:10:35.100 --> 04:10:41.100
One of these bills comes up. I know you're tired of me talking about it, but I don't bring these bills.

04:10:41.100 --> 04:10:46.100
I want to do things for Kansans, and that's not this.

04:10:46.100 --> 04:10:51.100
But our communities are afraid, and they're tired of watchness, make a mockery of the system.

04:10:51.100 --> 04:10:58.100
They're not having true bill hearings. You know, committee hearings where people can actually come and share their thoughts.

04:10:58.100 --> 04:11:03.100
And even when they do not being hurt or taken seriously.

04:11:03.100 --> 04:11:07.100
So, you know, I'll be done here, but I want you all to consider this for the future.

04:11:07.100 --> 04:11:13.100
This is not how we should be operating as a government. Nobody is really thinking this through.

04:11:13.100 --> 04:11:16.100
And I'm just done, but no.

04:11:16.100 --> 04:11:21.100
The chair recognizes representative Bieler for an announcement.

04:11:22.100 --> 04:11:25.100
Ten to Commerce fans.

04:11:25.100 --> 04:11:27.100
Just kidding.

04:11:27.100 --> 04:11:31.100
House Social Services Budget Committee. We are canceling today's meeting.

04:11:31.100 --> 04:11:35.100
So, 330 House Social Services Budget Committee is canceled.

04:11:35.100 --> 04:11:41.100
We will pick up tomorrow with our scheduled agenda and adjust as we need to.

04:11:41.100 --> 04:11:45.100
Thank you, Mr. Chair.

04:11:45.100 --> 04:11:48.100
Is there any other member wishing to speak to the bill?

04:11:48.100 --> 04:11:51.100
The chair recognizes representative Weiko.

04:12:05.100 --> 04:12:07.100
Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

04:12:10.100 --> 04:12:13.100
Will the carrier of the bill please stand for a question?

04:12:19.100 --> 04:12:27.100
I'm going to shift us back to the driver's license portion of this bill.

04:12:27.100 --> 04:12:28.100
All right.

04:12:28.100 --> 04:12:40.100
It's my understanding and I looked at the attorney general's testimony that he submitted at the hearing that one of the reasons for the initial legislation was because.

04:12:41.100 --> 04:12:43.100
Accuracy on driver's license was really important.

04:12:43.100 --> 04:12:44.100
Is that true?

04:12:44.100 --> 04:12:49.100
Particularly for people to be able to like identify somebody or see somebody.

04:12:49.100 --> 04:12:52.100
The initial, meaning the women's bill of rights?

04:12:52.100 --> 04:12:53.100
No, I'm sorry.

04:12:53.100 --> 04:12:57.100
The bill you heard the second day of session this year.

04:12:57.100 --> 04:12:58.100
Yes.

04:12:58.100 --> 04:13:00.100
It was for accuracy.

04:13:00.100 --> 04:13:01.100
All right.

04:13:01.100 --> 04:13:05.100
Okay. Thank you.

04:13:06.100 --> 04:13:07.100
Body.

04:13:07.100 --> 04:13:11.100
I stand in very, very strong opposition to this bill.

04:13:11.100 --> 04:13:25.100
However, if the supporters of this bill are truly concerned about the information on driver's licenses, then I think it's important we are consistent and we look at other descriptors on our driver's licenses.

04:13:25.100 --> 04:13:31.100
As I was thinking about this, I pulled out my driver's license, which frankly I hadn't looked at in a really long time.

04:13:32.100 --> 04:13:37.100
And I thought, I looked at what it said, I said, says my hair color is the same.

04:13:37.100 --> 04:13:41.100
I'm getting a little gray, maybe from this job, but generally it's the same.

04:13:41.100 --> 04:13:43.100
My eye color is the same.

04:13:43.100 --> 04:13:46.100
My height's the same.

04:13:46.100 --> 04:13:52.100
But guys, my weight is not the same.

04:13:52.100 --> 04:13:55.100
It's really inaccurate.

04:13:56.100 --> 04:14:10.100
I think the weight listed on my driver's license is so different from my actual weight that it actually might be hard for someone to use the information on my driver's license in order to identify me.

04:14:10.100 --> 04:14:23.100
In the attorney general's testimony in support of this legislation, it says this bill restores quote, uniformity and accuracy to state issued documents.

04:14:23.100 --> 04:14:35.100
I have an amendment.

04:14:35.100 --> 04:14:40.100
The amendment appears long. Is there objection to the reading of the amendment?

04:14:40.100 --> 04:14:51.100
There is objection the clerk will read.

04:14:51.100 --> 04:14:58.100
I move to amend house substitute for SB244 on page five following line four by inserting new section three.

04:14:58.100 --> 04:15:12.100
Any person applying for the issuance or renewal of a driver's license or a non drivers identification card shall be weighted at the location where such person is making such application or in lieu of being weighed in person.

04:15:12.100 --> 04:15:24.100
This person may submit documentation signed by a physician stating such person's weight provided such documentation was issued by such physician not more than six weeks prior to the date that such person submitting the application.

04:15:24.100 --> 04:15:38.100
The weight recorded or submitted with documentation pursuant to subsection A shall be the weight indicated on such person's driver's license or non drivers identification card and in all other information pertaining to such person that is reported by the division of vehicles.

04:15:38.100 --> 04:15:47.100
Section four, it shall be unlawful to have a difference in weight of more than 15 pounds from the weight stated on such person's driver's license or non drivers identification card.

04:15:47.100 --> 04:15:53.100
If a person's weight is different from the weight stated on such person's driver's license or non drivers identification.

04:15:53.100 --> 04:15:57.100
The objection to waving the reading has been lifted or withdrawn.

04:15:57.100 --> 04:16:01.100
Representative Michael, you may explain your amendment.

04:16:01.100 --> 04:16:03.100
Thank you, Mr Chairman.

04:16:03.100 --> 04:16:07.100
In the name of accuracy, this is what this amendment does.

04:16:08.100 --> 04:16:17.100
In order to ensure people have accurate weight listed on their driver's license, they will have to either use a scale at the DMV to provide an accurate weight.

04:16:17.100 --> 04:16:25.100
Or provide documentation from a physician that is no more than six weeks old that states their weight.

04:16:25.100 --> 04:16:31.100
Furthermore, I know there's been a lot of debate today about whether there's a fiscal note to this bill that we haven't seen.

04:16:32.100 --> 04:16:43.100
But in the case there is, it creates a fee fund to pay for renovations that will be needed to bathrooms and government buildings, and it funds that fee fund by the following ways.

04:16:43.100 --> 04:16:53.100
When someone renews their license, a fee will be assessed if a person's actual weight is more than 15 pounds different from the weight listed on their expiring license.

04:16:53.100 --> 04:17:03.100
Additionally, if someone has a weight fluctuation of more than 15 pounds, they will have to renew their license and the fee collected for these renewals will be allocated to the fee fund.

04:17:03.100 --> 04:17:14.100
And I'll note that there's an exception for someone who is pregnant or up to 12 months postpartum.

04:17:14.100 --> 04:17:28.100
I remember wish to speak to the amendment. The chair recognizes representative Meyer.

04:17:28.100 --> 04:17:35.100
Yeah, it may come as no surprise. I'm not really sure how I feel about this amendment y'all.

04:17:35.100 --> 04:17:45.100
I mean, you know, if it mentioned hair color too, we might have some real issues because my hair color is obviously different every week, right?

04:17:45.100 --> 04:17:49.100
What about piercings? I came back with like two new piercings on my face.

04:17:49.100 --> 04:17:55.100
Hey, my driver's license says I weigh 150. I don't really want that to change.

04:17:55.100 --> 04:17:59.100
I'm working my way down there, but we know it's not accurate.

04:18:00.100 --> 04:18:09.100
That's been on there. I think since I was about 19 years old. I mean, you don't even have to update it. What I want to step on a scale though in front of everybody.

04:18:09.100 --> 04:18:11.100
I'm not sure.

04:18:11.100 --> 04:18:12.100
I am.

