04:37:10.100 --> 04:37:19.100
And that group of people that they are actually afraid of are, and I intend no offense to the majority of this body, it's men.

04:37:19.100 --> 04:37:22.100
It's men that we are afraid of.

04:37:22.100 --> 04:37:33.100
I have spent my entire life from when I was old enough to walk and talk being afraid of being hurt by men.

04:37:34.100 --> 04:37:40.100
When I found out that I was pregnant, that I was having a daughter, I was joyful and she's amazing.

04:37:40.100 --> 04:37:50.100
And I love being a parent, but I was terrified of what could happen to my daughter at the hands of men.

04:37:50.100 --> 04:37:55.100
When I found out I was having a son, I was even more scared as someone who grew up with all sisters.

04:37:55.100 --> 04:37:59.100
I didn't know what I would do as a parent of a little boy.

04:37:59.100 --> 04:38:04.100
I wasn't afraid of bringing my son into the women's room without me.

04:38:04.100 --> 04:38:06.100
Where was I afraid of sending him?

04:38:06.100 --> 04:38:11.100
The men's room without me, his mother, to protect him.

04:38:11.100 --> 04:38:16.100
That is where the concerns of Mike's constituents are.

04:38:16.100 --> 04:38:18.100
They are not anti-trans.

04:38:18.100 --> 04:38:27.100
They are anti-men exploiting a loophole and using that to assault women and children.

04:38:27.100 --> 04:38:32.100
What's been interesting to me is that I've talked about this quite a bit.

04:38:32.100 --> 04:38:41.100
I am a history major and I love going down rabbit holes in particular when it comes to our duties as legislators.

04:38:41.100 --> 04:38:53.100
One of our most important duties as was stated by the Vice Chair of Judiciary is to make sure that our constituents are safe and that they have privacy.

04:38:54.100 --> 04:39:04.100
We're going to have to go back in time to look a little bit about the infrastructure of something that is a little bit icky to talk about, but every single one of us in this room do it.

04:39:04.100 --> 04:39:11.100
That is using the restroom or toileting as would be the proper terminology here.

04:39:11.100 --> 04:39:20.100
If you look at the history of public restrooms, public restrooms for men actually existed even as early as Mesopotamian times.

04:39:20.100 --> 04:39:36.100
You have seen a lot of archaeological artifacts where you have these public restrooms where it is several toilets together, no wall together, nothing like that, where you have a lot of men using the toilet together.

04:39:36.100 --> 04:39:38.100
Love that for you guys.

04:39:38.100 --> 04:39:45.100
It's not exactly the type of lack of privacy that I would prefer, but you see a lot of that.

04:39:46.100 --> 04:39:52.100
A lot of locker rooms or changing rooms or bathing facilities are also all for men.

04:39:52.100 --> 04:39:55.100
That goes back especially to Greco-Roman times.

04:39:55.100 --> 04:40:08.100
We won't speak about some of the consensual things that Greco-Roman folks engaged in and why anyone who would support such a lack of privacy might be in favor of that, but it can be heavily implied.

04:40:08.100 --> 04:40:16.100
You don't start seeing public restrooms for women until the late Victorian era.

04:40:16.100 --> 04:40:29.100
And I want you all, if you so desire, if you're interested in this urinary history lesson, is to go Google something called the urinary leash and separate spheres.

04:40:29.100 --> 04:40:49.100
Anyone who has taken a gender studies course knows that in the Victorian era and in eras before that women were primarily kept at home, not necessarily because people gave one gosh darn about our privacy or safety, but because we were property.

04:40:49.100 --> 04:40:56.100
And people did not want their property to be damaged, in other words, raped or assaulted.

04:40:57.100 --> 04:41:06.100
In late Victorian times, especially as the industrial revolution started coming up, you start seeing more public restrooms for women.

04:41:06.100 --> 04:41:13.100
And that is when you start seeing that extension of or that getting away from the separate spheres.

04:41:13.100 --> 04:41:23.100
The urinary leash actually existed because before there were public restrooms for women, there was only one place that we could go and that was at home.

04:41:23.100 --> 04:41:26.100
There were no public restrooms for us to go in.

04:41:26.100 --> 04:41:33.100
So you start seeing these public restrooms separated by gender for both men and women coming up.

04:41:33.100 --> 04:41:48.100
And for the most part, some of the arguments that I have heard my colleagues talking about today have been talking about very real fears that women and girls have of being assaulted in restrooms.

04:41:49.100 --> 04:42:03.100
And there seems to be a misconception stated where people say that just because you are in a single gender space that you are automatically safe.

04:42:03.100 --> 04:42:06.100
And I would argue that to the contrary.

04:42:06.100 --> 04:42:18.100
So, like many boomer and Gen X women, and I have talked with some of my female colleagues about this, I grew up in Johnson County and I attended public schools.

04:42:18.100 --> 04:42:29.100
And one of the things that I had to do because my teacher made me and made my other classmates do this in order to get a grade was that in my all female locker room.

04:42:30.100 --> 04:42:43.100
So you really didn't have, at least at my time, was not aware of any transgender or gender nonconforming students who would have been in the restroom with me in the late 80s or in the locker room with me in the late 80s.

04:42:43.100 --> 04:42:48.100
But by God, if you think that I was safe in that locker room, think again.

04:42:49.100 --> 04:43:02.100
My gym teacher forced us to undress in our locker rows and then walk completely nude to a shower that we had to take our grade was based on this.

04:43:02.100 --> 04:43:08.100
And then we had to go back to our lockers with a towel about the size of a Kleenex.

04:43:08.100 --> 04:43:10.100
It was horrific.

04:43:10.100 --> 04:43:12.100
I am still not okay.

04:43:12.100 --> 04:43:17.100
I mean, there are a lot of reasons why I'm not just to bring some levity, but that is one of them.

04:43:17.100 --> 04:43:23.100
And, but honestly, that is a huge problem.

04:43:23.100 --> 04:43:24.100
And you know what?

04:43:24.100 --> 04:43:28.100
All female space supposed to be super safe.

04:43:28.100 --> 04:43:46.100
And yet you have an adult female authority figure telling minor children that they have to undress and not just undress partially and change out for gym, but get all the way down to the nude and be in front of their minor classmates and in front of an adult.

04:43:46.100 --> 04:43:49.100
That is wrong.

04:43:49.100 --> 04:43:54.100
And in fact, a lot of school districts, thank God, are starting to phase this out.

04:43:54.100 --> 04:43:57.100
You're also starting to see issues with this in private schools as well.

04:43:57.100 --> 04:43:58.100
You can look up case law.

04:43:58.100 --> 04:44:01.100
There is a Catholic school that had issues with this.

04:44:01.100 --> 04:44:06.100
I want to say in Indiana that are starting to phase this out because you know what?

04:44:06.100 --> 04:44:13.100
Just being one gender together in a locker room does not make you safe.

04:44:13.100 --> 04:44:18.100
We also want to look at the way that we use the toilet differently.

04:44:18.100 --> 04:44:26.100
By necessity, it is going to take us ladies a little bit longer of an amount of time to use the restroom.

04:44:26.100 --> 04:44:27.100
We menstruate.

04:44:27.100 --> 04:44:29.100
We have to take our pants down.

04:44:29.100 --> 04:44:30.100
We have to sit down.

04:44:30.100 --> 04:44:37.100
It takes us a little bit of time to undress and to do our business in a sanitary and appropriate way.

04:44:38.100 --> 04:44:47.100
The public restrooms for men did not always have urinals, but the urinal was first patented in 1866, I believe, here in the United States.

04:44:47.100 --> 04:44:49.100
Although it was also widely used in France.

04:44:49.100 --> 04:44:51.100
Again, this is a thing that you know now.

04:44:51.100 --> 04:44:52.100
You're welcome.

04:44:52.100 --> 04:44:57.100
But the problem with urinals is this.

04:44:57.100 --> 04:45:02.100
