05:35:07.100 --> 05:35:13.100
if they couldn't print those copies and turn them in on time, they were still able to have their testimony sent to the committee.

05:35:13.100 --> 05:35:14.100
So I appreciate that.

05:35:14.100 --> 05:35:23.100
But our office riled up every office assistant and intern we could find to get Kansans testimony printed, copied, and turned in.

05:35:23.100 --> 05:35:31.100
If this isn't something that is so deeply unpopular to the public, then why are you doing it in a rushed and hidden process?

05:35:31.100 --> 05:35:37.100
Again, you have the numbers. You have a super majority that you expanded after the last election.

05:35:37.100 --> 05:35:40.100
You have the ability to pass these things.

05:35:40.100 --> 05:35:44.100
You have the ability to schedule a hearing, allow the public to come way in.

05:35:44.100 --> 05:35:48.100
And at the end of the day, we can get up here and debate and disagree.

05:35:48.100 --> 05:35:51.100
And that's how the democratic process is supposed to work.

05:35:52.100 --> 05:36:02.100
And so I hope and I know that the hour is long and people have been going all day and I feel for our revizers who stayed up all night and orally this morning getting these things done.

05:36:02.100 --> 05:36:11.100
But shoving bills like this through the process this quickly is wrong.

05:36:11.100 --> 05:36:16.100
I also heard a lot today about protecting Kansans.

05:36:16.100 --> 05:36:20.100
And my disagree with your approach to doing so.

05:36:20.100 --> 05:36:30.100
But through that, there is a very real situation if this bill is passed into law, where there is someone that does present as mail that shows up in a restroom.

05:36:30.100 --> 05:36:39.100
There is a reality in which someone who has transitioned in a female shows up in a men's restroom if they're complying with the law.

05:36:39.100 --> 05:36:46.100
In Kansas under our hate crime statutes, we penalize crimes at higher levels.

05:36:46.100 --> 05:36:55.100
If someone walks into a restroom and a trans man who is buff and bearded and they decide that they're frustrated and they're going to take matters into their own hands.

05:36:55.100 --> 05:37:08.100
Yes, it's a crime to assault someone, but doing so simply because of their gender identity or expression or sexual orientation should be included as an elevated level.

