05:53:03.100 --> 05:53:12.100
I sit on four committees. None of them are the queer committee.

05:53:12.100 --> 05:53:28.100
I've sat in a hearing about pesticides. I have never thought I would be more interested in pesticides than I was the past couple of days.

05:53:28.100 --> 05:53:52.100
I've sat in a hearing about adding fetal alcohol spectrum disorder to disabilities class so that students with FASD are able to access effective education.

05:53:52.100 --> 05:54:10.100
I've sat in hearings about whether we should allow chaplains either on a paid or voluntary status into our public schools to provide moral and religious support to our students.

05:54:11.100 --> 05:54:28.100
I sat in another hearing where we debated whether or not we were going to offer our Kansas students effective mental health services while they're in school.

05:54:28.100 --> 05:54:35.100
That's what I have done on my days outside of this chamber.

05:54:35.100 --> 05:54:43.100
In fact, today, this morning, I sat in a two hour hearing about crypto kiosks.

05:54:43.100 --> 05:54:51.100
And if anybody likes to go down a rabbit hole, I suggest that one.

05:54:51.100 --> 05:55:09.100
