05:55:10.100 --> 05:55:26.100
Our kids and parental rights and the right for parents to make good informed decisions about how they want their children to be raised.

05:55:26.100 --> 05:55:33.100
And then I come to the floor.

05:55:33.100 --> 05:55:43.100
And I've had the opportunity to vote on a performative bill to denounce the United Nations.

05:55:43.100 --> 05:55:53.100
A worldwide organization originally proposed by Franklin D. Roosevelt.

05:55:53.100 --> 05:56:08.100
That's a vote on a resolution for the Constitution of states, as if we're in some Orwellian version of Gone with the Wind.

05:56:08.100 --> 05:56:12.100
And then today.

05:56:12.100 --> 05:56:26.100
Now, while I am somewhat flattered that this chamber seems so obsessed with me.

05:56:26.100 --> 05:56:38.100
I want to take this opportunity to apologize to my constituents for this massive waste of time.

05:56:38.100 --> 05:56:41.100
And tax payer money.

05:56:41.100 --> 05:56:52.100
This bill, whether it passes or not, has already cost taxpayers thousands of dollars, all of us sitting here all day long.

05:56:52.100 --> 05:57:00.100
We've made a lampoon, a procedure and due process.

05:57:00.100 --> 05:57:20.100
And flippant arguments such as we've already talked about this before is not a legitimate reason to short circuit democracy.

05:57:20.100 --> 05:57:37.100
Now, I think my colleagues have aptly and repeatedly demonstrated through both their words and their votes that this bill is not about children's safety and privacy.

05:57:37.100 --> 05:57:44.100
It is not about women's safety.

05:57:44.100 --> 05:57:50.100
It's not about protecting victims of violence.

05:57:50.100 --> 05:57:55.100
It's certainly not about doing the business of the people.

05:57:55.100 --> 05:58:09.100
Even the arguments in favor of accurate documents to assist law enforcement are dubious at best.

05:58:09.100 --> 05:58:24.100
What this bill is about is about sending a very clear message to people who are transgender that you are not welcome and you are not safe here.

05:58:24.100 --> 05:58:48.100
It's about making participation in society as perilous and as punitive as humanly possible for transgender canons or just people who visit Kansas.

05:58:48.100 --> 05:58:57.100
I did not come here to debate my right to life.

05:58:57.100 --> 05:59:09.100
I came here because I live in a working class district and working class districts deserve working class representation.

05:59:09.100 --> 05:59:13.100
A little bit about my district.

05:59:13.100 --> 05:59:15.100
I'm from House District 86.

05:59:15.100 --> 05:59:20.100
That's in the southeast portion of Wichita.

05:59:20.100 --> 05:59:26.100
In my district, there are nine educational facilities.

05:59:26.100 --> 05:59:32.100
