05:59:32.100 --> 05:59:40.100
There are 1,400 veterans in my district.

05:59:40.100 --> 05:59:47.100
25% of the population of my district is Hispanic.

05:59:47.100 --> 05:59:56.100
District 86's median income is two thirds that of the average of Kansas and the United States.

05:59:56.100 --> 06:00:08.100
20% of my district lives below the poverty line and that includes 27% of children in my district.

06:00:08.100 --> 06:00:19.100
The high school graduation rate of my district is 80%.

06:00:19.100 --> 06:00:33.100
I am a college graduate who has chosen to stay in Kansas and do what I can to make this a great place to live.

06:00:33.100 --> 06:00:39.100
So amidst the ongoing brain drain of Kansas.

06:00:39.100 --> 06:00:44.100
Am I a boon to Kansas?

06:00:44.100 --> 06:00:49.100
Or am I a danger?

06:00:49.100 --> 06:00:53.100
I'm a United States Air Force veteran.

06:00:53.100 --> 06:01:02.100
And ever since Brownback rescinded protections for LGBTQ state employees.

06:01:02.100 --> 06:01:08.100
I have always wondered as a veteran, am I revered and honored?

06:01:08.100 --> 06:01:17.100
Or am I just disparaged and cast aside as a trans person?

06:01:17.100 --> 06:01:26.100
I'm an elected official, like almost everybody in this room.

06:01:26.100 --> 06:01:31.100
Am I afforded all of the rights and responsibilities of an elected official?

06:01:31.100 --> 06:01:43.100
Or do I need to just go waste my time at facilities asking where I'm allowed to take a dump?

06:01:43.100 --> 06:01:48.100
Regardless of the answer to those questions, I am here to do real work.

06:01:48.100 --> 06:01:52.100
I am here to find ways to keep Kansans in their homes.

06:01:52.100 --> 06:01:57.100
I'm here to make health care affordable and accessible for Kansans and their families.

06:01:57.100 --> 06:02:05.100
I'm here to hopefully strengthen public education for all of our children, including those in special ed.

06:02:05.100 --> 06:02:23.100
I'm here to advocate for a livable wage for Kansans so that they can afford the rising prices and costs of literally everything.

06:02:23.100 --> 06:02:33.100
We owe it to our constituents to spend our time and their treasure on laws that strengthen our families and our state as a whole.

06:02:33.100 --> 06:02:41.100
And not on culture war nonsense that pits Kansans against each other unnecessarily.

06:02:41.100 --> 06:02:55.100
I desperately want to believe that this collection of adults is astute enough to drop this bill, vote no, and focus on helpful legislation.

06:02:55.100 --> 06:03:01.100
Instead of harmful legislation, I guess we'll see.

